29	Open Badges v3	1EdTech Open Badges Specification v3.0 - a digital badge expressed as a W3C Verifiable Credential. Entities and attributes derived from the published AchievementCredential JSON schema (ob_v3p0_achievementcredential_schema.json). The root entity uses the specification's OpenBadgeCredential alias rather than AchievementCredential.	\N	SourceSchema	\N	Built by copying the 175 Open Badges 3.0 attributes already present in CLR v2 (DataModels.Id 3), which had been authored as a combined CLR/OB model, and adding the Related class from the spec. Excluded: the CLR-specific entities ClrCredential, ClrSubject and Association; the 12 CLR v2 attributes with no counterpart in the 3.0 schema; and Context and ProfileRef, which declare no properties of their own. Array flags on every type and @context attribute were set to Yes to match the spec's "MUST be an unordered set" wording, correcting 12 CLR v2 rows.	3.0	2026-08-20 14:49:19.831672+00	\N	\N	\N	LIF	f	Draft	\N	\N	\N	\N
14	CASE	1EdTech Competencies and Academic Standards Exchange (CASE) Service, Final Release v1.1 (24 Jan 2025, errata v1 13 Mar 2025). https://www.imsglobal.org/spec/case/v1p1	\N	SourceSchema	\N	Scope decisions (2026-08-07): (1) CFPckgDocument/CFPckgItem/CFPckgAssociation are not modeled as separate entities -- consolidated into CFDocument/CFItem/CFAssociation, which therefore carry the union of standalone + package-embedded fields (e.g. CFDocument.CFPackageURI, CFItem/CFAssociation.CFDocumentURI are present but optional even though CASE would omit them inside a CFPackage). (2) LinkURI/LinkGenURI are not modeled as entities -- all *URI-suffixed attributes (including originNodeURI/destinationNodeURI/subjectURI) are flat DataType=string scalars rather than {title,identifier,uri[,targetType]} objects; TargetTypeEnum is therefore also not modeled. (3) The 5 *Set collection wrappers, the 13 *Extension classes (and the extensions property on every class), and imsx_StatusInfo/imsx_CodeMinor/imsx_CodeMinorField are excluded entirely as transport/wrapper constructs with no competency content of their own.	1.1	\N	\N	\N	\N	LIF	f	Draft	\N	\N	\N	\N
6	Ed-Fi v5	\N	Required and Array in this model reflect element cardinality in the Ed-Fi v5.0.0 XML interchange schema (Ed-Fi-Core.xsd, targetNamespace http://ed-fi.org/5.0.0). This model describes the XML interchange representation, not the ODS/API REST/JSON projection, which expresses references, collections and choice constructs differently. Do not diff this model's cardinality against an ODS/API Swagger document - differences between the two are representational, not defects.	SourceSchema	\N	Tracks Ed-Fi Data Standard v5.0.0 (XSD targetNamespace http://ed-fi.org/5.0.0; source: tag v5.0.0 of Ed-Fi-Alliance-OSS/Ed-Fi-Standard). Ed-Fi Data Standard 5.1 and 5.2 exist as minor updates to the 5.x line and are not tracked by this model.	5.0.0	\N	\N	\N	\N	LIF	f	Draft	\N	\N	\N	\N
10	CTDL	Credential Transparency Description Language (CTDL), ceterms namespace, as published by Credential Engine.	\N	SourceSchema	\N	Rebuilt 2026-11-02 from CTDL-authority-20260927.json (credreg.net CTDL JSON-LD with meta properties, release 20260927; SHA-256 5d4410b2350e62a39bd0a57dffec2bcf7c34183102a0a821fdd88b74dd6c4ff9): 140 classes, 418 properties, 7,753 domain rows, 36 concept schemes, 457 concepts; plus the deprecated ceterms:Competency and ceterms:CompetencyFramework retained by decision. Generator, rules and verification: projects/lif_mdr_database/data_models/ctdl/ in the lif-core repository.\nArray on attribute rows follows `multivalue` in CTDL-registry-publishing-schema.json (Credential Registry publishing schema; SHA-256 ae2d046ec8e93884006a413ea795e63485d3d48fad7616a21dd742f3e58638e0), not CTDL, which declares no cardinality. The three attribute rows whose property the Registry lacks carry Array null. Every association carries a boolean Array: on an attribute association it mirrors the attribute row (false where that is null); on a reference association it follows the property's multivalue (false where the Registry lacks the property), which the association Notes also record.\nRequired exists solely so references render: the schema generator copies only a referenced entity's required properties. ctid and name are Required wherever present, with a substitute pair on classes that have neither. Required does not assert CTDL cardinality.\nEvery domain row with an in-model class range is a Reference association named by the property; its child is one of the permitted targets (listed in the association Notes), chosen by build_ctdl_model.py. Every other row is an attribute, one row per class and property, UniqueName <Class>.<property>.\nClass hierarchy is recorded in each entity's Notes as subClassOf lines; foreign parents are marked.	1.0	\N	\N	\N	\N	LIF	f	Draft	\N	\N	\N	\N
4	CEDS v14	\N	CEDS declares no cardinality: Required and Array are not set on any element, and every association has Array false. A property whose range is a CEDS class is a Reference association named by the property, not an attribute. Class hierarchy (rdfs:subClassOf) is recorded in entity Notes, not as associations, and properties are not inherited down it.	SourceSchema	\N	Tracks CEDS Ontology v14.0.0.0 (released 2026-03-11; terms namespace https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/; owl:versionInfo 14.0.0.0). Built from CEDS-Ontology-v14.0.0.0.rdf (CEDStandards/CEDS-Ontology, tag V14.0.0.0, src/CEDS-Ontology.rdf; SHA-256 26d782b6047236e84ba181f1ee38030560fad65e2cce9b47acc5062c212255e3) and cross-checked against CEDS-V14.0.0.0.xlsx (CEDStandards/CEDS-Elements; SHA-256 a92c2d4239dc682ac408de94e728c368196d47b71199f78288db8414cdc1f523); the RDF is the authority where the two disagree. ISO6393LanguageCode is capped using the Part1 column of SIL's iso-639-3.tab (SHA-256 07ce5fed94472312bdd1a4bd7f297c83e7cd4ac4ff335dfbed0824a270f482ed). Generator, rules and verification: projects/lif_mdr_database/data_models/ceds/ in the lif-core repository.	14.0.0.0	\N	\N	\N	\N	LIF	f	Draft	\N	\N	\N	\N
