18286	1261	A graphic order interaction is a graphic interaction with a corresponding set of choices that are defined as areas of the graphic image. The candidate's task is to impose an ordering on the areas (hotspots). The order hotspot interaction should only be used when the spatial relationship of the choices with respect to each other (as represented by the graphic image) is important to the needs of the item. Otherwise, orderInteraction should be used instead with separate material for each option.	\N	GraphicOrderInteraction	Graphic Order Interaction	\N	CEDS v14	concept: NI001158104272	\N	\N	\N	\N	LIF	f	\N	f	4
18287	1261	In an order interaction the candidate's task is to reorder the choices, the order in which the choices are displayed initially is significant. By default the candidate's task is to order all of the choices but a subset of the choices can be requested using the maxChoices and minChoices attributes. When specified the candidate must select a subset of the choices and impose an ordering on them.	\N	OrderInteraction	Order Interaction	\N	CEDS v14	concept: NI001158104279	\N	\N	\N	\N	LIF	f	\N	f	4
18288	1261	A graphic associate interaction is a graphic interaction with a corresponding set of choices that are defined as areas of the graphic image. The candidate's task is to associate the areas (hotspots) with each other. The graphic associate interaction should only be used when the graphical relationship of the choices with respect to each other (as represented by the graphic image) is important to the needs of the item. Otherwise, associateInteraction should be used instead with separate Material for each option. SliderInteraction -- The slider interaction presents the candidate with a control for selecting a numerical value between a lower and upper bound. It must be bound to a response variable with single cardinality with a base-type of either integer or float.	\N	GraphicAssociateInteraction	Graphic Associate Interaction	\N	CEDS v14	concept: NI001158104274	\N	\N	\N	\N	LIF	f	\N	f	4
